---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Sky Serpent — CopperTrace"
  description="A modular RF sensing research platform combining embedded receiver nodes, SDR, Ethernet infrastructure and automated signal analysis."
>
  <article class="article">
    <div class="article-meta">Project 002 · Active R&amp;D</div>
    <h1>Sky Serpent</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      A modular RF sensing research platform exploring how embedded receiver nodes,
      software-defined radio and centralised analysis can be combined into repeatable,
      evidence-driven RF experiments.
    </p>

    <div class="callout">
      This public overview intentionally stays at system level. Detailed detection signatures,
      raw captures, datasets and implementation-specific classification methods are kept private
      while the research develops.
    </div>

    <h2>Research objective</h2>
    <p>
      Sky Serpent investigates RF-based detection and characterisation in complex radio
      environments. The emphasis is not simply on observing RF energy, but on building the
      tools needed to collect repeatable measurements, compare observations and evaluate
      techniques for reducing false positives.
    </p>

    <div class="diagram" role="img" aria-label="Sky Serpent high-level architecture">
      <div class="diagram-title">HIGH-LEVEL ARCHITECTURE</div>
      <div class="diagram-row">
        <div class="diagram-node">RF environment</div>
      </div>
      <div class="diagram-arrow">↓</div>
      <div class="diagram-row diagram-split">
        <div class="diagram-node">Embedded sensor nodes</div>
        <div class="diagram-node">SDR sensing</div>
      </div>
      <div class="diagram-arrow">↘ &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Ethernet &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; ↙</div>
      <div class="diagram-row">
        <div class="diagram-node diagram-accent">Labrax analysis infrastructure</div>
      </div>
      <div class="diagram-arrow">↓</div>
      <div class="diagram-row diagram-split">
        <div class="diagram-node">Evidence capture</div>
        <div class="diagram-node">Analysis &amp; comparison</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>Modular sensing</h2>
    <p>
      The platform separates sensing from central analysis. Small network-connected nodes can
      concentrate on acquiring observations while Linux systems handle storage, comparison,
      visualisation and more computationally expensive processing.
    </p>
    <p>
      One established development path uses embedded Ethernet-connected receiver hardware for
      analogue 5.8 GHz experiments. The wider platform also incorporates software-defined radio
      for research that requires access to raw RF/IQ information.
    </p>

    <h2>Controlled RF laboratory</h2>
    <p>
      A detector is difficult to evaluate when the transmitted signal is unknown. Sky Serpent
      therefore includes controlled, low-power test infrastructure so experiments can be repeated
      against known conditions and the resulting observations retained for later comparison.
    </p>

    <div class="diagram" role="img" aria-label="Controlled RF test workflow">
      <div class="diagram-title">EVIDENCE-FIRST TEST LOOP</div>
      <div class="diagram-flow">
        <div class="diagram-node">Known test condition</div><div class="diagram-arrow-inline">→</div>
        <div class="diagram-node">RF observation</div><div class="diagram-arrow-inline">→</div>
        <div class="diagram-node">Capture</div><div class="diagram-arrow-inline">→</div>
        <div class="diagram-node">Compare</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>Current focus</h2>
    <div class="fact-grid">
      <div class="fact"><strong>Embedded sensing</strong><span>Modular Ethernet-connected receiver architecture.</span></div>
      <div class="fact"><strong>SDR integration</strong><span>Extending experiments beyond dedicated receiver hardware.</span></div>
      <div class="fact"><strong>Evidence capture</strong><span>Retaining measurements and test context for repeatable analysis.</span></div>
      <div class="fact"><strong>Automation</strong><span>Building repeatable test and collection workflows.</span></div>
    </div>

    <h2>Research direction</h2>
    <p>
      Current research areas include signal characterisation, multi-sensor correlation,
      classification, distributed sensing and false-positive reduction. These are research
      directions rather than claims of completed capability.
    </p>

    <h2>Why build it?</h2>
    <p>
      Sky Serpent is as much a systems-engineering project as an RF project. It brings together
      electronics, embedded firmware, networking, SDR, Linux infrastructure, signal analysis and
      automation while keeping each layer measurable and replaceable.
    </p>

    <div class="callout">
      The aim is not to start with a predetermined answer about what can be detected. The aim is
      to build the tools required to measure it and find out.
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
